WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.182 --> 00:00:01.896
When should AI say, I don't know?

2
00:00:02.115 --> 00:00:04.916
In mammography, making uncertainty visible

3
00:00:04.916 --> 00:00:07.023
could change how people use advice.

4
00:00:07.321 --> 00:00:10.980
Eleven radiologists read sixty selected mammograms,

5
00:00:11.025 --> 00:00:12.716
across three sessions:

6
00:00:12.993 --> 00:00:16.790
no AI, standard AI, and safety-zone guidance.

7
00:00:17.078 --> 00:00:18.792
The prediction stayed the same.

8
00:00:19.011 --> 00:00:21.836
Added guidance marked rule-in, rule-out,

9
00:00:22.078 --> 00:00:24.984
and a gray zone where human judgment remained primary.

10
00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:29.365
Median reader sensitivity rose from eighty percent with standard AI

11
00:00:29.468 --> 00:00:32.004
to ninety percent with safety-zone guidance.

12
00:00:32.303 --> 00:00:36.007
Among gray-zone cases, median joint reader-AI failure

13
00:00:36.007 --> 00:00:38.809
fell from fifty percent to twenty-five percent.

14
00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:41.920
This small, enriched pilot needs validation

15
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.016
in representative screening populations.

16
00:00:44.366 --> 00:00:47.203
Make uncertainty actionable. Support judgment.

17
00:00:47.422 --> 00:00:49.576
Help people know when to rely on AI.
